---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is this legal?',
    a: 'ani-sdk resolves publicly accessible stream URLs from sites that host content openly on the web. It does not bypass DRM, decrypt proprietary streams, or circumvent paywalls. How you use the resolved URLs is your responsibility.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work in the browser?',
    a: 'No. ani-sdk requires Node 20+ or Bun. It uses crypto.subtle for AES-CTR decryption and shells out to curl as a fallback transport — neither is available in a browser context. For browser clients, run the HTTP server and call it over HTTP.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when a provider goes down?',
    a: 'Each provider is independently swappable. If one source changes its API or goes offline, you swap the provider import — the three calls (search, fetchContentUnits, resolveStream) stay identical. The live E2E test suite catches upstream changes automatically.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need FlareSolverrClient for basic use?',
    a: "No. None of the three built-in providers (AllManga, Gogoanime, Goyabu) require FlareSolverrClient. It's an optional transport for custom providers that target Cloudflare or DDoS-Guard protected sites.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What does resolveStream actually return?',
    a: "A ResolvedMediaStream discriminated union — all current providers return type: 'video'. The streams array holds IVideoPayload objects: each has a sourceUrl, an isHLS boolean, a quality string, and optional headers the CDN requires. See the API reference for the full types.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I add my own provider?',
    a: 'Yes. Extend BaseProvider, implement the three methods, re-export from src/index.ts, and add one live E2E test. The contributing guide walks through each step with code examples.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does ani-sdk support downloading?',
    a: 'No — ani-sdk returns stream URLs. Downloading is out of scope. Feed the resolved URL to ffmpeg, yt-dlp, or any other tool that accepts HLS or direct video URLs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between sub, dub, and raw?',
    a: "sub = original audio with subtitles (default). dub = audio dubbed into another language (usually English). raw = original audio with no subtitles. Providers that don't support a requested language fall back to sub.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How are providers tested?',
    a: 'Each provider has a live E2E test that searches a real show, resolves a real stream, fetches a segment ~5 seconds in, and runs ffmpeg to extract a PNG frame. The assertion is that the frame is larger than 1 KB. No mocking — the point is to catch upstream site changes.',
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <div class="font-sans text-white">
    <div class="frame">
      <Nav />

      <div class="hline px-10 py-8">
        <div class="label mb-3">FAQ</div>
        <h1 class="mb-2 text-[32px] font-bold tracking-tight">Frequently asked questions.</h1>
        <p class="text-[14px]" style="color: var(--muted);">
          Answers to common questions about ani-sdk. Missing something?
          <a
            href="https://github.com/hexxt-git/ani-sdk/issues"
            target="_blank"
            class="underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-white"
            >Open an issue.</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <div class="hline px-10 py-6">
            <div class="mb-2 text-[14px] font-semibold">{faq.q}</div>
            <p class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 680px;">
              {faq.a}
            </p>
          </div>
        ))
      }

      <Footer />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
